      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BRUCE WAYNE (4) was in the money on debut then started long odds but ran well above expectations, breaking through for maiden win by a nose at this track over 530m (31.15). Rates a top chance and can measure up again. TERRIFIC DAVE (1) drew this same box last time when a 5 length winner (22.52) in a Grade 6 over 395m at Murray Bridge. Harder here but expected to feature again. BEAMING (7) has an excellent record over this course and distance having never missed the placings in five starts, including three wins and two placings. Was out of the placings last time (23.27) at Gawler in a Special conditions race, finishing fourth and beaten 5.5 lengths. Can feature in the finish. TERRIFIC NERO (8) won in the best time of the program last time out. Hard to beat again.",
